-- title:
--   Future false endpoints under the ordered Cauchy–Schwarz stage map
-- statement:
--   Let $r,s,N$ be natural numbers, put $m=r+s+2$, choose $j\in\{0,\ldots,m-1\}$, and let $x:\{0,\ldots,m-1\}\times\{0,1\}\to\mathbb Z/N\mathbb Z$ be a cube point. Write $\Phi_{r,s,N,j}$ for the ordered Cauchy–Schwarz stage equivalence, $f_t$ for its future-coordinate index, and $\sigma_j$ for the increasing map skipping $j$. For every $0\le t<s$, the corresponding future coordinate in the false-endpoint component is
